WEBVTT

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.730
Welcome, Selector.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.900
Give me a name.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.140
Selector?

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.110
A name?

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.210
Yes.

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:14.490
Give me a name.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:18.990
Meru.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.000
Girl / Ideal and Reality

00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:56.170
How many Selectors are there?

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.470
I don't know.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.310
Where can I find them?

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:02.460
Hmm... I don't know.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:09.920
Hey, you really can find them, can't you?

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.950
Yes. As long as they're close.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.320
When they are, tell me.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.060
You're so optimistic.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:17.760
It's just a game, right?

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.700
I just want it over with.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.320
I'm back!

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:24.340
Welcome back.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:25.950
You've been getting home late, huh?

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.620
Yeah, work's been busy.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.540
Have you eaten?

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:30.980
I have.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.420
Oh, Mom...

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.940
Can I ask for a midnight snack?

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.860
We have proficiency tests tomorrow.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:38.940
Sure.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:41.840
Hey.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.920
Aren't you going to study 
WIXOSS today, Chi-chan?

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.850
Stop calling me that.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.060
You used to like being called that.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.950
<b>Monthly Proficiency Test 

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.120
Chinatsu, how'd it go?

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.990
Okay, I guess.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.520
I don't know about that second math problem.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.000
You say that, but you're trying 
for the top ten, aren't you?

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.130
I am.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.540
I'm so jealous.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.510
You're sure to get the special scholarship.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.500
I want to eat something sweet!

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.260
Let's go!

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.740
Sorry, I have work.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:26.780
See you tomorrow.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:30.890
Welcome.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.900
Thank you.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.450
One more day?

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.280
The new girl quit.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.440
Didn't you want as many shifts as possible?

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:47.790
I guess five days a week is too much, huh?

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.450
You've got school, too.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.290
I'll do it.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.210
Wow!

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.590
I'm so jealous, Chi-chan.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.840
You're good at studying and the bar, too.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.760
You'll learn to do it soon.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.600
Let's practice together.

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.980
O-Okay.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.110
Hang in there, Suzu!

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.880
I know you can do it.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:25.860
Give it one more try!

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:27.890
Okay.

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.040
Build up a lot of momentum.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:33.540
Up, and...

00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:36.880
See? You did it!

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:38.840
Yeah, I did it!

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:46.500
Someday, I'm going to be like you, Chi-chan.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.000
Huh?

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.090
I like you the way you are.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.380
No! I'm gonna be like you!

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.070
Hang in there.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:09.960
Hey, Chinatsu!

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.720
Let's walk together for a bit.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:16.960
Dad, you're leaving early today?

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.110
Yeah.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.200
There's some work I didn't quite finish.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.990
If this job goes well, I could get 
promoted to project lead.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:25.800
Really?

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:30.840
If my salary goes up, it would 
help pay for your tuition, right?

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.080
Yeah.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:34.730
Your company?

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.810
We have to sell the house?

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.150
We can't do anything?

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:41.730
I'm sorry...

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:43.220
I'm sorry!

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:47.110
Chinatsu worked hard to get into 
a good private school, too!

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.910
I want to be like you, Chi-chan.

00:05:55.880 --> 00:05:58.500
I won't give up.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.300
All right, take care.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.110
Okay. Bye.

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:16.580
Chi-chan...

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:18.210
Stop calling me that.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.650
A Selector is coming from the front.

00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:28.740
You're a Selector, aren't you?

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.950
Will you have a battle with me?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.430
If you like.

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.170
Meru?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:49.930
It's all right.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.890
She's just unconscious.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:57.150
You're holding yourself back.

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.810
That's why you lost.

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.900
Why didn't you use your coin?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.300
I told you about it yesterday.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.320
I don't like the idea of 
controlling people's minds.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:14.810
Is it cowardly?

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.180
Would Suzu hate you?

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:21.040
She wants to be you, right?

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.540
I want to win fair and square, 
with my own power.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.140
But you lost.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.300
Two more losses, and you'll disappear.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:31.290
I just need to take it back, right?

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.340
Ener Charge?

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:36.180
Lancer...

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:36.890
<b>Code Order Steak      Associated Card Code Eat Teaksauce 

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:37.700
I see...

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:39.930
So you can build your deck like this?

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.930
You're not scared of the game?

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:42.920
Not really.

00:07:43.390 --> 00:07:44.560
It's just a game, right?

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.700
I just want this to be over with.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:53.860
Magazine Corner

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.620
<b>WIXOSS Card Encyclopedia V</b>

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.060
A Selector is here.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.080
Oh? Chinatsu?

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:09.900
We're coming from cram school.

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:10.900
What about you?

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:13.420
Your job isn't around here, is it?

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.300
Oh, well...

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:17.070
WIXOSS?

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:19.390
Sorry, I'm in a hurry!

00:08:24.240 --> 00:08:26.520
Too bad. Looks like they're gone.

00:08:34.150 --> 00:08:38.910
<b>WIXOSS Card Encyclopedia V        For a Better Night's Sleep</b>

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:36.650
"Build the perfect deck...

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:39.220
Find the SIGNI that's right for you."

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.250
This is too complicated for me.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.400
Suzuko?

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:49.500
D-Don't talk to me when people are around.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.860
They'll think I'm weird.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:54.970
Only Selectors can hear my voice.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:58.120
More importantly, you seem to have a visitor.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:08:59.400
A visitor?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.310
Discovered.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:04.390
Homura Suzuko-san, from class 2-C?

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:07.640
How did you know my name?

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.360
I research my enemies.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:12.980
Your enemies?

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.180
Apologies.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:16.100
I haven't introduced myself.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:19.340
I'm Mikage Hanna, from class 1-A.

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.700
Mikage Hanna-san...

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.420
Astonishment!

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:26.460
Did you read my review?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.250
<b>Doctor Hanna</b>

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:36.190
"Doctor Hanna's Game Review"?

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:50.150
Um... Even if you follow me, I won't battle you.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.130
Doubt.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:56.140
You won a battle and went from 
one coin to two, didn't you?

00:09:56.140 --> 00:09:57.400
Right, Anonymous-chan?

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.560
That's correct, Hanna-sama.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.160
She has two coins that shine like the sun!

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:03.550
Anonymous-chan?

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:04.830
Conclusion.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:08.120
You have no reason to avoid 
a battle with me now, do you?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.920
But if I lose, I'll be back to one!

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:15.090
If you have an article in a game magazine,

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.980
you must be really strong.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:19.510
Obviously. I will win.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:23.510
I really don't want to fight.

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:25.930
Inexplicable.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.480
Understood.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:30.000
I'll make the offer again some other time.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.690
Um... Hanna-san, aren't you scared?

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:35.140
Denial.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.660
There are two reasons I fight.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:40.020
First, as a game writer,

00:10:40.020 --> 00:10:42.910
I'm simply interested in Selector battles.

00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:47.250
And the second is that there's 
a memory I want to manipulate

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:50.710
as the reward for winning the battle.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.620
Farewell.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.010
See you around.

00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:00.200
Riru...

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.070
If you win the battle,

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.550
you don't just get to quit?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.360
As a reward,

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:10.310
you can change one of your memories 
to whatever you want.

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:12.020
A memory?

00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:16.970
Erase it, alter it, restore it,

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:19.780
or even create a memory 
that didn't previously exist.

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.330
If you want.

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.480
If I...

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:35.420
<b>Private</b>

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:43.140
<b>22      Morikawa Chinatsu</b>

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:44.880
Morikawa.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.350
Can I talk to you?

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:50.310
Morikawa, weren't you interested 
in the special scholarship?

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:51.660
Yes.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.320
It would mean free tuition.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.770
That won't happen with these grades.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:00.940
You're still working that part-time job, 
right? How many days a week?

00:12:01.230 --> 00:12:02.420
Five days a week.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:03.950
Five days, huh?

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:08.160
Can't you cut back a little and study more?

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:14.790
If my salary goes up, it would 
help pay for your tuition, right?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.040
I'll talk... to my parents.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:19.580
Good.

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:22.510
Oh, and I wanted to check something.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:26.910
There's a rumor that you've 
been out late at night.

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:28.220
Is that true?

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.500
That's a lie! Who said—

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:39.730
Well, I'm sure it's a mistake. 
But I know you want that scholarship.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:51.330
Um, you're a Selector, right?

00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:53.580
How late do you work?

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.770
When you're done, do you want to battle?

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:59.320
How many times have you battled?

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:01.220
This'll be my third time.

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:04.270
So far, I've lost one and won one. 
What about you?

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:06.020
Do I need to tell you?

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:07.220
Oh, right.

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.780
I guess that'd be useful information.

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:12.180
Kagari, they're waiting for you.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.740
Oh, sorry.

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:14.520
Then...

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:16.220
Open!

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:24.740
Meru, attack.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:28.280
All right.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.200
Yukime, are you okay?

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:31.320
Yes.

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:33.830
It seems she'll be using standard attacks.

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:35.330
Turn end!

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:39.620
My ability will be effective against her.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:40.590
Got it.

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.180
Coin bet!

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:44.620
Predict.

00:13:48.940 --> 00:13:50.460
She used her coin.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:52.290
What kind of ability is it?

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:53.280
I don't know.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.750
It's your turn.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.890
<i>I can't attack recklessly.</i>

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:57.880
Draw!

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.570
<b>Code Eat Hambur             Servant O</b>

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:02.690
I can see them!

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:05.340
Servant and Hambur.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:08.070
Hambur is strengthened when it's accessorized.

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:09.910
That's bad, isn't it?

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:10.570
Don't worry.

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:13.320
We can handle it with the cards we have.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:14.580
That's her power?

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.360
Play two Ketchu.

00:14:17.360 --> 00:14:17.910
Attack!

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:19.450
Kagari, this is your chance.

00:14:19.450 --> 00:14:20.310
Yeah.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:23.220
I use Three Burning Gathered 
Steps to banish all of them!

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:30.650
You won't use your coin?

00:14:31.650 --> 00:14:33.480
Meru, attack.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.560
All right! My second win!

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:45.940
Well, don't be so down.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.280
I'm sure you'll win next time.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:50.490
Okay, bye!

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:54.830
You only have one coin left.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.540
Meru, you said that if I lose all my coins,

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:00.390
I'll disappear, right?

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:01.080
Yes.

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:03.240
What did you mean?

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:06.560
What disappears?

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.930
You can't mean... that I'll disappear?

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.260
But this is just a game, right?

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:18.200
That's why I thought I just had to end it...

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:19.520
That's why...

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:20.810
You just have to win.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.540
You can win, Chi-chan.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:24.310
Aren't you the one Suzu wants to be?

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:24.310
Stop it.

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:26.970
She always looked up to—

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:27.320
I said stop it!

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:31.570
You're not Suzu.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:33.080
Suzu...

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:33.950
A Selector is here.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:34.990
Behind you.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:36.700
Walking toward you.

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.580
They noticed you.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:43.540
Morikawa?

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:45.770
Oh, it's her?

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:48.550
She's a Selector, huh?

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.460
Chinatsu, morning.

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:55.780
Too bad about the procifiency test.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:58.350
It's the first time you've 
ranked in the 20s, right?

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.060
Want to have a consolation party?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.440
That's a great idea!

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.020
Do you have work today?

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:05.960
What are you doing?!

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.490
Stop it, Morikawa!

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:14.400
Why did you do that? Don't you understand?

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:17.090
If your behavior is bad, 
you can't get that scholarship.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:18.620
I won't apologize.

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:19.860
Morikawa...

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:20.960
I won't apologize!

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.750
What? Why?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:25.220
Oh, well...

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:28.880
You caused a problem at school, didn't you?

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:30.620
That's...

00:16:30.620 --> 00:16:34.990
We can't hire someone like that 
and have something happen.

00:16:35.900 --> 00:16:40.500
I mean, you're a hard worker, 
and we've been really glad to have you,

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.270
but I'm sorry. Today's your last day.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.480
That was their plan from the start.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:49.260
Once the project got going, 
there was no need for me.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:51.390
Then, this company-owned house, too?

00:16:51.390 --> 00:16:51.940
Yeah.

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:54.040
We leave at the end of the month.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:02.340
Hang in there.

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:03.780
Hang in there.

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:04.840
Hang in there!

00:17:04.840 --> 00:17:06.480
I know you can do it.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:07.710
Give it one more try!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.830
Someday, I'm going to be like you ... chan.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:14.550
Huh?

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.600
I like you the way you are.

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.220
No! ...gonna be like you.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.280
Hang in there?

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:23.900
Why should I hang in there?

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.700
Because she wants to be like me?

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:28.650
Who does?

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:29.980
Suzu?

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:32.870
Hello!

00:17:33.580 --> 00:17:35.570
You're a Selector, right?

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:37.730
Will you have a battle with me?

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:39.030
Please!

00:17:40.300 --> 00:17:41.370
Chi-chan.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.420
All right.

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:48.210
Yay!

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:49.420
Okay...

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:50.630
Open!

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:04.930
You only have one coin, huh?

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.990
Poor thing.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:09.090
Maybe I'll lose for you...

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:09.850
That's a lie!

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:11.610
I'm going to win!

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.070
Hey, Rio-chan...

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:15.520
Only bad girls lie.

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.530
I'm sorry, Onee-san.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:19.360
Right, good girl.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.200
Meru, grow.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.500
Place the SIGNI. Turn end.

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:27.960
It's my turn.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.540
Okay, Mommy, grow!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.750
Right, right.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.630
I play her and her... and turn end!

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.550
Rio-chan, what about your attack?

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.650
I forgot! What do I do?!

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:43.160
She's a funny girl, huh?

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:44.900
All right, it's our turn.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:45.860
R-Right.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.060
Meru, grow.

00:18:47.910 --> 00:18:49.610
Attack with all SIGNI.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.150
Something really strong is coming!

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:57.440
Turn end.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.130
It's our turn, Rio-chan.

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.530
Then I'll use my coin.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:02.700
Bet!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.140
All right.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:06.340
Cheating.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:10.970
Then I play her and her, and I'm done.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:10.970
What was that?

00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:12.840
It looked like she used a power.

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:13.710
I don't know.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:15.170
For now, attack.

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:17.670
<b>Formula of Philosophical Wisdom    # Descartes #</b>

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:21.050
Yes!

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.340
Surprised you, huh?

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:23.860
My plan worked!

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.640
The ability to set bombs?

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:27.310
She has that kind of power?

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:30.600
That was great acting, Rio-chan.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.590
Really?

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:32.770
Now it's my turn to attack.

00:19:33.030 --> 00:19:34.310
Mommy, grow!

00:19:35.450 --> 00:19:37.720
Fermat and Descartes, attack!

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:44.820
Attack.

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:49.660
Meru!

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:01.090
Hey, Chi-chan...

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:03.460
You won't use your coin?

00:20:04.060 --> 00:20:06.760
At this rate, you'll lose.

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:09.050
Lose?

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:10.730
Me?

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:13.190
Your company?

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:12.980
<i>No.</i>

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:14.780
...a consolation party?

00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:16.150
<i>No. No...</i>

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:16.610
Today's your last day.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.740
<i>No! No! No! No!</i>

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:19.660
<i>No!</i>

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:22.460
I...

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:25.070
I won't lose.

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:31.080
Coin bet!

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:37.780
<i>I can feel them...</i>

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:39.330
<i>Chi-chan's memories.</i>

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:40.980
<i>Her emotions.</i>

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:44.840
Berserk.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.230
Mommy... Mommy!

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:02.690
Mommy! Mommy!

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.280
Wow, Chi-chan.

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:12.170
You were so cool during that fight.

00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:14.030
You looked so alive!

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:17.440
I could feel your strength and your feelings.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:19.290
Alive?

00:21:19.820 --> 00:21:23.260
I want to be like you.

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:26.050
I want to be like you!

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:33.020
I forgot about Suzu...

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:34.980
Chi-chan?

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:40.110
A good student. A hard worker.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:42.020
Always right.

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:48.510
Who am I hanging in there for?

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:52.450
Do I...

00:21:53.940 --> 00:21:55.600
really need Suzu?

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:29.210
Doubt. Are you afraid to lose?

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:31.980
I intend to keep running until the 
time limit's up, without fighting.

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:34.560
Do you really know what 
it means to disappear?

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:34.980
I don't have time!

00:23:34.980 --> 00:23:37.860
So that's what it means to disappear?

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:37.860
As long as the two of us are together, it's okay.

00:23:37.860 --> 00:23:40.940
Next time: Selector / Honey and Poison.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:40.940
Selector / Honey and Poison
